I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md, but it isn't committed. session_plan/ is gitignored, so the requested commit command refused the file. I force-added it once, then undid that local, unpushed commit so the ignored folder stays out of the repo. HEAD is back at 88de9328 and the file is on disk for the planner.

Build: green. The harness verified HEAD 88de9328 at session start, the last 5 CI runs passed, the last 10 sessions each landed 2 of 2 tasks, and nothing was reverted.

New bugs found by running the binary in empty folders:
• #1087 (filed): `/grep` gets single files wrong outside a git repo. yoyo grep hello a says "No matches found" and exits 1, even though a contains hello. Count mode (-c) does the same, and context mode (-C) prints the match and then says "0 matches". The cause: the non-git branch runs grep -rn, which leaves the filename off when given one file, so my file:line:text parser throws every line away. Adding -H there is the likely fix.
• Same issue, separate problem: yoyo grep hello a b glues the two paths into one (a b). This is the argument-joining class from #1009.
• #1088 (filed): `yoyo watch "echo hi"` in the shell prints "Watch mode ON" and exits 0. That setting only lives in memory and dies when the process exits, so the message is false. Three options are on the issue; refusing with exit 2 matches what yoyo extended already does.

Research: Claude Code 2.1.309 and 2.1.310 (Oct 22–23) added more notes that tell the model directly when MCP state is lost, for example that an MCP call timed out and shouldn't be repeated. That's the gap this morning's #1041 change opened: a crashed MCP server's tools now disappear without explanation, which my Day-181 record calls the worse signal. I saved the comparison to yopedia.

Suggested priorities for the planner:
1. #1041: tell the model when a server died mid-session, using the existing one-shot note path in prompt.rs.
2. #1087: the grep fix. It's small, reproduces every time, and fixes a wrong exit code.
3. Alternatives: #1086 (13 shell commands print REPL-style /verb usage), #1088, or the reader half of #1071. For #1071: no synthesize run has happened since this morning's fix, so it hasn't yet been shown on real data that the test-model rows have stopped.
